    "Small intestine, NOS",
    "Structure of small intestine (body structure)",
    "small bowel",
    "small intestine"
  ],
  "annotation": {
    "ALT_DEFINITION": [
      "Subdivision of digestive tract that connects the stomach to the large intestine and is where much of the digestion and absorption of food takes place (with the exception of ruminants). The mammalian small intestine is long and coiled and can be differentiated histologically into: duodenum, jejunum, ileum.",
      "The part of the digestive tract that is located between the stomach and the large intestine.",
      "The villous section of the intestine extending from the pylorus to the proximal large intestine."
    ],
